      "lesson_abacus_count_on_make_ten": "Show 6 on the ones rod. Add 2 by sliding two more earth beads (8). Now try 9 + 4. The ones rod cannot hold 13, so use 4 = 10 − 6: push up one earth bead on the tens rod (+10), then take 6 off the ones rod (lift the heaven bead and drop one earth bead). The abacus reads 13.",
      "lesson_place_value_one_million": "A thousand-cube is 1,000. Ten of those make 10,000. A hundred of those make 100,000. A thousand of them make 1,000,000: picture a giant cube 10 thousand-cubes long, 10 wide and 10 tall. Now you understand \"one million.\"",
