      "hawking_radiation": "Hawking radiation",
      "henrietta_leavitt": "Henrietta Leavitt: ",
      "henrietta_swan_leavitt": "Henrietta Swan Leavitt",
      "hercules": "Hercules",
      "hercules_cluster": "Hercules Cluster",
      "hercules_cluster_m13": "Hercules Cluster (M13)",
      "here_is_the_puzzle_quantum_mechanics_s": "Here is the puzzle. Quantum mechanics says information is NEVER lost — the state of a closed system evolves unitarily, and you can always reconstruct the past from the present if you have full information. But Hawking's calculation says the radiation coming out of a black hole is purely thermal — random, carrying no information about what fell in. If the black hole eventually evaporates completely into thermal radiation, the information about everything that fell in is GONE. Unitarity violated. The two pillars of modern physics, GR and QM, are giving incompatible answers. Hawking himself stated in 1976 that information IS lost. Most physicists came to believe that cannot be right; the resolution must be that the radiation carries information in some subtle way Hawking's leading-order calculation missed.",
