      "rr_lyrae_globular_cluster_ageometers": "RR Lyrae — globular-cluster ageometers",
      "rr_lyrae_variables_named_for_rr_lyrae_": "RR Lyrae variables (named for RR Lyrae, the prototype) are SHORTER-PERIOD pulsators (0.2-1 day) common in old globular clusters. They are all about the same intrinsic brightness (~ 40 times the Sun), so each one acts as an INDEPENDENT distance indicator. RR Lyrae are particularly useful for distances to old populations + for galactic-archaeology work. They are easy to find (their distinctive sawtooth light curves stand out) + bright enough to be detected throughout the Milky Way halo + into nearby galaxies. Over 50,000 RR Lyrae are now catalogued; current + future surveys (Gaia, LSST) will find millions.",
