      "deck_replacement": "Deck replacement",
      "deep_beam_approximation": "⚠ Deep-beam approximation. ",
      "deflection": "Deflection δ",
      "demolition_as_engineering_education": "Demolition as engineering education",
      "dense_sand_gravel": "Dense sand + gravel",
      "depth_mm": "Depth (mm)",
      "design_brief": "Design brief",
      "design_brief_copy": "Start by stress-testing a bridge, then use material and force references only when you need evidence for a redesign.",
      "design_cycle": "Design Cycle",
      "design_for_disassembly": "Design for disassembly: ",
      "design_name": "Bridge design name",
      "design_name_e_g_marie_s_pedestrian_bri": "Design name (e.g., \"Marie's pedestrian bridge over Back Cove\")",
      "design_note_no_numeric_safety_factor_t": "Design note: no numeric safety-factor target, no reveal button, no quiz validation. Safety is shown as a discrete 3-state marker (SAFE / MARGINAL / FAILS), not a continuous gradient — by design, to discourage optimization-gaming behavior. The point is the inquiry, not the number.",
      "design_notes": "Design notes",
      "design_parameters": "Design parameters",
      "design_readiness": "Design readiness",
      "design_specific_elements_to_yield_defo": "Tsim cov thaj tsam tshwj xeeb, zoo li cov pob qij plastic ntawm ncej, kom khoov hla ntau zaug thiab tso zog tawm. Lwm cov feem raug tsim los tiv thaiv cov zog uas cov thaj tsam ntawd xa tau. Qhov no txo tau kev pheej hmoo pob, tab sis kev puas tsuaj mus tas li tej zaum yuav tshwm sim.",
      "design_the_structure_to_elastically_re": "Muab lub zog txaus rau cov av qeeg uas npaj tseg, nrog cov pob qij thiab kev txhawb nqa tsim zoo. Kev txhawb ib feem muaj zog tuaj tej zaum yuav ua rau lub zog nce hauv cov feem nyob ib sab, yog li cov kws tsim kuaj tag nrho txoj kev nqa hnyav.",
      "distance_from_epicenter_km": "Distance from epicenter (km)",
      "distributed_fiber_optic_sensing": "Distributed fiber-optic sensing",
      "drilled_shafts_caissons": "Drilled shafts (caissons)",
      "driven_piles": "Driven piles",
      "drone_based_inspection": "Drone-based inspection",
      "ductility_the_modern_approach": "Kev khoov tau tsis lov: ",
      "earthquake_magnitude_m_w": "Earthquake magnitude (M_w)",
      "ec_factor": "EC factor",
      "element_types_you_will_meet": "Element types you will meet",
      "embodied_co": "Embodied CO₂",
      "endurance_limit_steel_only": "Endurance limit (steel only): ",
      "energy_dissipation_dampers": "Energy dissipation + dampers",
      "energy_release": "Energy release",
      "engineering_design_structural_mechanic": "Engineering Design · Structural Mechanics · NGSS HS-ETS1 + HS-PS2",
      "engineering_is_iterative_you_design_te": "Engineering is iterative. You design, test, fail, learn, redesign. Failure is information, not defeat. Every working bridge in the world is the descendant of many failures.",
      "engineering_is_learned_at_least_as_muc": "Kev kawm tsim khoom kawm tau los ntawm kev swb ntau npaum li los ntawm kev yeej. Kev pob ntawm Tacoma Narrows tau hloov txoj kev tsim choj ntev; kev vam meej ntawm Brooklyn ua pov thawj tias choj dai nyob tau tshaj ib puas xyoo.",
      "engineering_responses": "Engineering responses",
      "environmental_community_impact": "Environmental + community impact",
      "environmental_justice_community_impact": "Environmental justice + community impact",
      "erasmusbrug": "Erasmusbrug",
      "eug_ne_freyssinet_france_1928_gustave_": "Eugène Freyssinet (Fabkis, 1928) + Gustave Magnel (Belgium, 1940s) tau tsim pob zeb nias ua ntej (prestressed concrete). Txoj kev no xav tau xov hlau muaj zog heev — hlau qub tsis muaj zog ncab tsawg dhau tsis tuav tau kev nias thaum pob zeb nqis. Tam sim no yog qauv thoob ntiaj teb rau choj luv thiab nruab nrab. Choj Confederation (Canada, 12.9 km ntawm pob zeb nias ua ntej) + ntau tug choj hla kev loj Asmeskas yog pob zeb nias ua ntej.",
      "every_bridge_built_today_is_analyzed_w": "Every bridge built today is analyzed with FEA somewhere in its design. It is the workhorse method, the reason engineers can design structures the hand-calculation generation could not. It is also the easiest tool in engineering to use badly. Both are worth understanding.",
      "every_bridge_eventually_retires_the_ho": "Every bridge eventually retires. The how + why is its own engineering discipline — explosive demolition for unconstrained sites, mechanical saw-cut work in dense urban settings, piece-by-piece retirement of bridges that must stay in service during their own replacement. Environmental recycling, community impact, historical significance, + research opportunities all factor in. A bridge's last project is rarely simpler than its first.",
      "every_bridge_has_an_engineering_story_": "Every bridge has an engineering story + a money story. Where the dollars come from, who decides what gets built, how contracts are awarded, who benefits from the project, who pays the maintenance — these questions shape what bridges actually exist + which communities get to use them. Engineering does not happen in a political vacuum + students who understand only the technical side will struggle to advocate for the bridges their communities need.",
      "every_bridge_stands_on_something_the_s": "Txhua tug choj sawv rau saum ib yam dab tsi. Tus nqaj muaj zog tshaj uas tus kws tsim zoo tshaj tsim yeej pob yog lub HAUV PAUS pob. Xyoo 1987 Choj Schoharie Creek pob thaum dej nyab tshoob av hauv qab ib tug ncej, thiab xyoo 1989 choj Hatchie River pob tom qab tus dej hloov kev mus tsoo nws cov ncej. Lwm qhov kev pob, zoo li 1907 Choj Quebec (cov hlau nias khoov) thiab 1967 Choj Silver (ib tug hlau eyebar tawg), pib nyob rau saum choj, yog li txhua feem ntawm txoj kev nqa hnyav tseem ceeb. Kev kawm av + kev tsim hauv paus tseem ceeb npaum li kev tsim saum choj.",
      "every_material_has_tradeoffs_strength_": "Every material has tradeoffs. Strength, weight, cost, durability, environmental impact. The right material depends on the structure and the context.",
