      "the_three_sisters_de_oh_h_ko_meaning_t": "The Three Sisters (De-oh-há-ko, meaning “they sustain us” in Haudenosaunee) is an ancient agricultural system with roots in Mesoamerica, where maize was domesticated about 9,000 years ago. Indigenous agricultural science developed sophisticated polyculture techniques long before modern ecology.",
