      "bar_lever": "Bar (lever)",
      "bar_width_relative_speed_log_scale_eac": "Bar width = relative speed (log scale; each tick is roughly 10× faster than the one above). Print was a step change — about 2× faster than horse-only, plus the ability to multiply copies at each relay stop. The bigger change came later (telegraph, internet). But print is when the curve first bent up.",
