      "both_campaigns_are_about_active_stewar": "Both campaigns are about active stewardship of physical Maine landscape: fire on the barrens, water in the streams. Both involve Wabanaki-led work as the historical and ongoing foundation. Both reward you for matching technique to season and to specific zones. Mosaic's riparian zone (sweetgrass, beaver) is literally the same physical place as Watershed Steward's floodplain wetlands.",
      "both_cultural_mosaic_and_climate_pathw": "Both Cultural Mosaic and Climate Pathways center Indigenous-led work as foundational. Mosaic IS Wabanaki practice; Pathway's Climate Justice sector has the largest feedback-rule reach (low support there drags every other sector down). What pattern do you notice about how systems perform when Indigenous leadership is centered versus appended?",
