      "car2_d2_shop": "Start a side shop",
      "car2_d2_shop_d": "Keep the day job; spend about {value1} on a truck + equipment and build your own customers.",
      "car2_earn_intro": "A transparent model of three paths from age 18 to 40: pay, raises, overtime, tuition and student-loan interest. Every number it shows comes from the formulas listed under the chart. The settings are representative, not a forecast for you.",
      "car2_earn_intro_t": "Apprenticeship, college program or 4-year degree: who is ahead, and when?",
      "car2_earn_reset": "↺ Reset to representative settings",
      "car2_earn_title": "Earnings + debt explorer",
      "car2_edit_aria": "Path whose settings the sliders change",
      "car2_edit_label": "The sliders below change the settings for:",
      "car2_f_cum": "Cumulative net = the running sum of (year pay − loan payment). Break-even = the age where two running sums are equal.",
      "car2_f_debt": "Debt at graduation = each year's tuition, borrowed at the start of that year, grown at the loan rate until you finish school.",
      "car2_f_example": "Worked example: ",
      "car2_f_example_body": "{value1}, first year of full-time work (age {value2}): {value3}/hr × 2,080 h = {value4}; overtime {value5}; loan payment {value6}; net for the year {value7}.",
      "car2_f_left": "Left out on purpose: taxes, rent and food (everyone pays those), grants and scholarships (they shrink the debt), part-time work in school, benefits and pensions.",
      "car2_f_pay": "Year pay = wage × 2,080 h + 1.5 × wage × overtime hours × 52 weeks (overtime only on the hourly paths).",
      "car2_f_pmt": "Loan payment = D × r ÷ (1 − (1 + r)⁻¹⁰), paid every year for 10 years after school (standard repayment).",
      "car2_f_raise": "Wage in working year n = starting wage × (1 + raise)ⁿ. Raises compound, so a bigger raise matters more every year.",
      "car2_f_rep": "Representative 2025-26 figures, not a forecast: check current job postings, BLS Occupational Outlook data and each school's net-price calculator.",
      "car2_f_title": "How the model works (every formula)",
