      "insp2_col_weld": "Weld",
      "insp2_cq1": "Where do you look up the visual inspection acceptance criteria: undercut, porosity, undersized fillets?",
      "insp2_cq1_n1": "Fabrication covers how to make the weld (fit-up, preheat, workmanship), not how to accept it.",
      "insp2_cq1_n2": "Design sizes the weld on the drawing; it does not judge a finished weld.",
      "insp2_cq1_n3": "Qualification tests WPSs and welders, not production welds.",
      "insp2_cq1_why": "Clause 8 Inspection holds the acceptance criteria, including the visual table (Table 8.1) used on the Inspector's Bench.",
      "insp2_cq2": "A new welder must pass a 3G plate test before working on the job. Which clause governs the test?",
      "insp2_cq2_n0": "Fabrication is about production work, not qualification tests.",
      "insp2_cq2_n2": "Inspection includes checking that welders are qualified, but the test rules themselves are in Clause 6.",
      "insp2_cq2_n3": "Prequalification exempts some WPSs from testing; it never exempts welders.",
      "insp2_cq2_why": "Clause 6 Qualification covers WPS qualification and welder performance qualification: test positions, specimens and the ranges each test qualifies.",
      "insp2_cq3": "You are writing a prequalified WPS and need the minimum preheat for 1-1/2 in A572 Grade 50.",
      "insp2_cq3_n0": "Fabrication says preheat must be applied and kept up, but the prequalified minimum values are tabulated with the prequalification rules.",
      "insp2_cq3_n1": "Design does not set preheat.",
      "insp2_cq3_n3": "That clause covers existing structures, not new fabrication.",
      "insp2_cq3_why": "Clause 5 Prequalification of WPSs holds the prequalified minimum preheat and interpass table, with the other conditions a prequalified WPS must meet.",
      "insp2_cq4": "You need the rules for tack welds, cleaning between passes and controlling distortion.",
      "insp2_cq4_n0": "Inspection checks the result; how to make the weld is a workmanship rule.",
      "insp2_cq4_n1": "Prequalification lists joint details and conditions for prequalified WPSs, not shop workmanship.",
      "insp2_cq4_n2": "Stud welding is a special process with its own clause.",
      "insp2_cq4_why": "Clause 7 Fabrication covers workmanship: preparing base metal, assembly, tack welds, cleaning, distortion control and repairs.",
      "insp2_cq5": "Shear studs are being welded to a beam flange for a composite floor. Where are the stud rules?",
      "insp2_cq5_n1": "Tubular Structures covers pipe and HSS connections.",
      "insp2_cq5_n2": "Design may call for the studs, but how to weld and test them is in Clause 9.",
      "insp2_cq5_n3": "General fabrication rules do not cover the stud welding process.",
      "insp2_cq5_why": "Clause 9 Stud Welding has its own rules for studs, including qualification, production tests such as bending a stud, and inspection.",
      "insp2_cq6": "An engineer wants to weld cover plates onto a 1970s building beam so it can carry more load.",
      "insp2_cq6_n0": "Fabrication is written for new work; existing structures have their own clause.",
      "insp2_cq6_n2": "Design rules apply to the new plates, but the existing-structure requirements sit in Clause 11.",
      "insp2_cq6_n3": "Qualification still applies to the welders, but it does not cover working on an old structure.",
      "insp2_cq6_why": "Clause 11 Strengthening and Repair of Existing Structures covers evaluating old steel and welding on structures already in service.",
      "insp2_crit_one": "{value1} at {value2}",
      "insp2_crit_pores": "worst inch {value1}; total {value2}",
