      "insp2_fb_wrong": "❌ The correct call is {value1}.",
      "insp2_fl1": "Draft WPS (often called a pWPS): the engineer writes the proposed settings.",
      "insp2_fl2": "Weld a test coupon following the draft, recording the actual values used.",
      "insp2_fl3": "Test the coupon: tension and bend tests, plus impact or hardness tests when the job requires them. A failed test sends you back to step 1.",
      "insp2_fl4": "PQR: the record of what was actually welded and the test results, certified by the employer.",
      "insp2_fl5": "Qualified WPS: the instructions welders follow, with ranges the PQR supports.",
      "insp2_fl6": "A welder welds a test coupon following the WPS.",
      "insp2_fl7": "The coupon is bend-tested or radiographed, as the code allows. A failure means retraining and a retest.",
      "insp2_fl8": "WPQ: the record that this welder is qualified, for that process, position and thickness range.",
      "insp2_fl_crack": "Surface crack (open to the surface)",
      "insp2_fl_lam": "Lamination (inside the plate, parallel to the surface)",
      "insp2_fl_lof": "Lack of fusion (flat, along the bevel face, inside)",
      "insp2_fl_poro": "Porosity (rounded gas pores inside the weld)",
      "insp2_flow_aria": "Flow diagram. Top row, the procedure: 1 draft WPS, 2 test coupon, 3 mechanical tests (a failure loops back to 1), 4 PQR. An arrow leads down to the bottom row, the welder: 5 qualified WPS, 6 welder test coupon, 7 bend test or radiograph (a failure loops back to 6), 8 WPQ.",
      "insp2_flow_h": "🔁 From a draft procedure to a qualified welder",
      "insp2_flow_key": "Orange row: the procedure (the recipe and its proof). Blue row: the welder (the license). Dashed red = a failed test sends you back.",
