      "low_hydrogen_electrodes_e7018_stored_h_r2": "Low-hydrogen electrodes (E7018, kept in a rod oven). Preheat to slow the cooling rate (prevents martensite). Stress-relief PWHT or a hydrogen bake-out where the procedure calls for it.",
      "lower_weld_quality_class_b_by_us_navy__r2": "Lower weld quality, usually qualified to Class B under AWS D3.6M (the Underwater Welding Code). Hydrogen embrittlement risk. Practical depth limit ~100 ft. Lower pay than hyperbaric.",
