      "met2_goto_haz_cool": "See what preheat does to cooling → HAZ Explorer",
      "met2_goto_heat": "Open the Heat Input Calculator →",
      "met2_goto_insp": "How inspectors find HAZ cracks → Inspection",
      "met2_goto_insp_short": "How cracks are found → Inspection",
      "met2_goto_ss": "Read: Stainless sensitization →",
      "met2_goto_underwater": "Wet welding quenches even faster → Underwater",
      "met2_haz_intro": "Each point in the base metal gets ONE peak temperature as the arc passes. Read that peak against the iron-carbon diagram and you know which zone the point lands in.",
      "met2_haz_takeaway": "For arc welds the visible HAZ is usually only a few millimetres (about 1/16-1/4 in) past the fusion line. At these settings the model puts it at {value1} mm ({value2} in). More heat input widens it; thicker plate narrows it. Notches, sharp corners and weld toes inside the HAZ are stress raisers where cracks start, so inspectors check this band with magnetic-particle (MT) or dye-penetrant (PT) testing.",
      "met2_haz_title": "🔥 HAZ Explorer — map the zones from peak temperature",
      "met2_hi_capped": "This explorer runs 5-100 kJ/in, so it uses {value1}.",
      "met2_hi_defaults": "No saved Heat Input Calculator settings, so its defaults were used: {value1}, {value2} V, {value3} A, {value4} in/min → {value5} kJ/in net.",
      "met2_hi_import": "⚡ Use my Heat Input Calculator settings",
      "met2_hi_imported": "Imported {value1}: {value2} V, {value3} A, {value4} in/min → {value5} kJ/in net.",
      "met2_lam_body": "A stepped, terrace-like crack INSIDE thick rolled plate, parallel to its surface, under a weld that pulls on the plate through its thickness (T- and corner joints). Rolled-flat inclusions are the weak planes. Fix: through-thickness (Z-grade) plate, buttering the plate face first, or a joint that does not pull through the thickness.",
      "met2_lam_head": "🪵 Lamellar tearing",
