      "met2_model_adams": "Thin plate (Adams): Tp = peak temperature Y mm past the fusion line, T0 = preheat, Tm = 1510 °C, ρC = 0.0044 J/mm³·°C for steel, t = thickness in mm, H = net heat input in J/mm. Thick plate uses Rosenthal's 3-D peak, Tp − T0 = H / (4.27·ρC·r²), with r measured from the weld centre.",
      "met2_model_auto": "Auto (hotter of the two)",
      "met2_model_caveat": "Conduction-only estimates for a single pass on steel. Real welds add joint shape, multiple passes and changing properties with temperature, so treat the millimetres as representative.",
      "met2_model_head": "📐 The model behind the picture",
