      "run_canvas_review": "Finished bead over {value1} in. of joint. Selected slice at {value2} in. is {value3}.",
      "run_canvas_run": "Torch running along the joint. The live numbers are in the readouts below.",
      "run_card_b1": "Travel speed is your live control (arrow keys or sliders)",
      "run_card_b2": "Thickness step, fit-up gap, stickout drift, heat build-up, tack weld",
      "run_card_b3": "Scored on % of bead length in spec, plus penetration, uniformity and defects",
      "run_card_b4": "Slice-by-slice review, prediction check and coaching; best saved per tier",
      "run_card_desc": "The torch lays a bead along the joint on its own. You steer travel speed (plus amps and volts) to keep penetration in spec while the plate thins from 1/4 in. to 1/8 in., a fit-up gap opens, your stickout drifts and the plate heats up. Every 0.05 in. of bead is graded on penetration and defects: your score is the share of the bead in spec, with sub-scores for penetration, uniformity and defects. An after-action review walks the bead slice by slice. Three tiers: Apprentice, Pro, Bath Iron Works. Personal best saved per tier.",
      "run_card_desc_r3": "Steer travel speed, amps and volts as plate thickness, fit-up and stickout change during a live pass. Inspect the recorded bead, pin one moment and compare its cross-section and readings with another. Three tiers: Apprentice, Pro and Bath Iron Works. Personal bests are saved per tier.",
      "run_card_subtitle": "Hold the bead in spec as the joint changes",
      "run_card_title": "Live Bead Run",
