      "sym2_mq2_why": "Triangles on BOTH sides of the reference line = weld on both sides. Same 1/4 size on each. Continuous (no length number).",
      "sym2_mq3_n1": "Fillets have no depth number; the numbers on the right are length and pitch.",
      "sym2_mq3_n3": "Amperage is never on a weld symbol; it belongs in the procedure (WPS).",
      "sym2_mq3_n4": "Pitch is centre-to-centre spacing, not overlap.",
      "sym2_mq3_o1": "3/16 fillet, 2\" long, 6\" deep",
      "sym2_mq3_o2": "3/16 fillet, intermittent 2\" long welds, 6\" pitch (center-to-center)",
      "sym2_mq3_o3": "3/16 fillet, 2 welds at 6 amps",
      "sym2_mq3_o4": "3/16 fillet, 2\" long welds overlapping each other by 6\" at every joint corner",
      "sym2_mq3_why": "Numbers to the right of the symbol are length-pitch: 2 in welds spaced 6 in centre to centre. Intermittent welding saves filler and heat input on long fillets.",
      "sym2_mq4_n1": "There is no V-shaped fillet, and penetration is never a percentage on the symbol.",
      "sym2_mq4_n2": "A bevel has one vertical leg; this symbol has two angled legs, and it sits below the line (arrow side).",
      "sym2_mq4_n4": "Welding position is not shown on the symbol; the angle is the groove angle.",
      "sym2_mq4_o1": "V-shaped fillet, 60% penetration",
      "sym2_mq4_o2": "Bevel weld, 60° included angle, other side",
      "sym2_mq4_o3": "V-groove weld, 60° groove angle, arrow side",
      "sym2_mq4_o4": "Vertical weld, 60° from horizontal",
      "sym2_mq4_why": "Two angled lines meeting at a point on the line = V-groove. The number with ° is the groove angle: the included angle of the whole V. Below the line = arrow side.",
      "sym2_mq5_n1": "A root opening is fit-up information; it does not change the required strength.",
      "sym2_mq5_n2": "The angle stays 60°; the 1/16 is a gap, written inside the symbol.",
      "sym2_mq5_n3": "Root reinforcement is not called out this way; the number inside the symbol is the gap.",
      "sym2_mq5_o1": "The weld is now stronger",
      "sym2_mq5_o2": "The bevel angle drops to 1/16 of 60°",
      "sym2_mq5_o3": "1/16\" of root reinforcement is required on the back side of the joint",
      "sym2_mq5_o4": "The plates are placed 1/16\" apart at the root before welding",
      "sym2_mq5_why": "Root opening = the gap between the two members at the root of the joint before welding. It is written inside the groove symbol. A small gap helps the root pass penetrate fully.",
      "sym2_mq6_n2": "The circle changes where the weld runs, not its size or shape.",
      "sym2_mq6_n3": "The weld follows the joint, whatever its shape; the circle only says go all the way around.",
      "sym2_mq6_n4": "Electrode choice is set in the procedure, never by a symbol shape.",
      "sym2_mq6_o1": "Weld extends completely around the joint (weld-all-around)",
      "sym2_mq6_o2": "Weld a circle of metal 1/4 thick around the base as a reinforcing collar",
      "sym2_mq6_o3": "This is a circular weld pattern",
      "sym2_mq6_o4": "Use a round electrode",
      "sym2_mq6_why": "An open circle at the reference-line/arrow junction = weld-all-around. Common for pipe-to-plate, post bases and gusset attachments.",
      "sym2_mq7_n1": "Inspection holds go in the notes or the tail.",
      "sym2_mq7_n3": "Electrode coatings are never shown on a symbol.",
      "sym2_mq7_n4": "Sign-off rules live in the quality plan, not in the flag.",
      "sym2_mq7_o1": "This weld must be inspected before next operation",
      "sym2_mq7_o2": "This weld is made in the field (not in the shop)",
      "sym2_mq7_o3": "This is a black-coated electrode weld",
      "sym2_mq7_o4": "Welder must sign off on this weld",
      "sym2_mq7_why": "Flag = field weld. It tells the shop NOT to make this weld: it is made at the install site, which changes equipment and procedure choice.",
      "sym2_mq8_n1": "One V cannot sit on both sides of the line; two symbols mean two grooves, each 60°.",
      "sym2_mq8_n2": "The symbols describe groove preparations, not individual beads.",
      "sym2_mq8_n4": "A bevel has a vertical leg; these are Vs, on both sides.",
      "sym2_mq8_o1": "Single V-groove with a 120° included angle on the arrow side",
      "sym2_mq8_o2": "Two separate 60° beads",
      "sym2_mq8_o3": "Double V-groove (V from both sides) with 60° angle each",
      "sym2_mq8_o4": "A 60° bevel from arrow side only",
      "sym2_mq8_why": "A V on BOTH sides of the line reads as an X: a double-V groove. Each V has a 60° groove angle, so each plate edge is cut at 30°. Used on thick plate where a single V would need too much filler.",
      "sym2_mq9_n1": "Weld time is never written in a tail.",
      "sym2_mq9_n2": "Quality grades are not shown this way.",
      "sym2_mq9_n3": "Travel speed belongs in the WPS, and 22 here is a document number.",
      "sym2_mq9_o1": "A 22-second welding time",
      "sym2_mq9_o2": "The weld is graded GT-22 quality",
      "sym2_mq9_o3": "Travel speed of 22 inches per minute using a gas-tungsten (GTAW) torch",
      "sym2_mq9_o4": "Use TIG (GTAW) process per Welding Procedure Specification #22",
      "sym2_mq9_why": "The tail of a weld symbol references documents. GTAW = the process. WPS-22 = a specific written procedure that defines the exact parameters (volts, amps, gas, technique).",
      "sym2_mq_final": "Quiz finished: {value1} of {value2} on the first try.",
      "sym2_mq_good": "Strong reading. Now write symbols yourself in the Symbol Builder.",
      "sym2_mq_lib": "Open the symbol library →",
