      "mo_heat_aria": "Bar chart of heat stress each year in Degree Heating Weeks, with guide lines at 4, 8 and 12. {severe} years reached 8 or more.",
      "mo_heat_label": "DHW",
      "mo_herbivores": "Protection for grazing fish",
      "mo_interval_end": "Years between severe heatwaves, by year 30",
      "mo_interval_now": "Years between severe heatwaves, at the start",
      "mo_intro": "This is a simplified teaching model of one reef. Each year it adds up heat stress, coral loss, coral regrowth, seaweed growth, grazing and anything people do to help. Pick a scenario, predict, then run it. Most scenarios start from a reef with 40% live coral; the rubble field starts almost bare.",
      "mo_leg_severe": "Severe heatwave year (8 or more Degree Heating Weeks)",
      "mo_leg_without": "Live coral on the same reef without the actions",
      "mo_leg_year": "The year you picked below",
      "mo_legend": "Chart key",
      "mo_limit_1": "Real reefs are made of many coral species that react differently. Here all coral is one number.",
      "mo_limit_2": "Regrowth is matched to one reef (Scott Reef, Australia) and coral death to one heatwave (Great Barrier Reef, 2016). That is why you can switch to a tougher reef.",
      "mo_limit_3": "Storms, disease and crown-of-thorns starfish are lumped into one small yearly loss. Heat stress is one number per year.",
      "mo_limit_4": "The grazing and runoff numbers are illustrative, and the switch to seaweed is sharper than on most real reefs.",
      "mo_limit_5": "Corals may adapt to warmer water over time. The model does not include that.",
      "mo_limit_6": "Heatwave timing is randomized. Use \"Run again\" to see how much the timing alone changes the result. This is a teaching model, not a forecast for any real reef.",
      "mo_limits_title": "What this model leaves out",
      "mo_mark_text": "Year {n}: live coral {c}%, seaweed {a}%",
